    <catchword>que</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">semper fugere teneri. Ratio 1.</l>
    <l n="2">est, quia ille extra culpam con-</l>
    <l n="3">stituitur, qui aliter adversus</l>
    <l n="4">vim &amp; injuriam se tueri non</l>
    <l n="5">potuit, quam id faciendo quod</l>
    <l n="6">fecit. Verùm qui loco consistit,</l>
    <l n="7">non aliter se potuit tueri. Igi-</l>
    <l n="8">tur &amp; extra culpam eo casu</l>
    <l n="9">constituetur. Ratio 2. est. Quia</l>
    <l n="10">nemo tenetur tale evadendi</l>
    <l n="11">medium eligere, quod sibi</l>
    <l n="12">maxime periculosum est, &amp;</l>
    <l n="13">quo electo, in majus sæpissime</l>
    <l n="14">periculum inciderer. Verùm</l>
    <l n="15">qui fugit, medium evadenti</l>
    <l n="16">maxime periculosum eligit.</l>
    <l n="17">Ergo. Unde etiam in jure nul-</l>
    <l n="18">libi dicitur, quod quis fugere</l>
    <l n="19">teneatur, verum tantum quod</l>
    <l n="20">periculum effugere debeat. Id-</l>
    <l n="21">que non tam fugiendo, quam</l>
    <l n="22">avertendo malum illatum, ad-</l>
    <l n="23">versarium vulnerando, aut ne-</l>
    <l n="24">cando. Quid, quod ideo dixe-</l>
    <l n="25">ro, neminem præcise fugere te-</l>
    <l n="26">neri, quod ipsa fuga quando-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The numeral after "Ratio" in the first instance is printed as a dotless i (ı), read here as 1. Ink spots on the page are stains and are not transcribed. Long s is rendered as s throughout.</notes>
